# control85.rc with the ABI changed to wasm64, and nothing else. Every other
# setting is byte-for-byte control85's so the only variable is the pointer width.
#
# It answers ONE question: what does a Drupal heap peak at when zend_long is 64
# bits. Measured struct growth is Bucket 24 -> 32, zend_string header 20 -> 32,
# HashTable 44 -> 56, zend_object 48 -> 56, zval unchanged at 16. The consumer's
# margin is 22.13 MiB against a 105.88 MiB authenticated render, so break-even is
# a blended +20.9% -- which falls BETWEEN zend_object and HashTable, so the mix
# decides it and the mix is unmeasured. Score it with
# worker/scripts/measure/growth-ladder.ts on the AUTHENTICATED render; a plain
# render reads 96.00 MiB on every arm and answers nothing.
#
# What it buys is PHP_INT_SIZE=8. It buys no address space: workerd caps linear
# memory at 128 MiB per isolate and enforces it by making grow() throw, so a
# declared maximum is not an allocated one.
#
# MEMORY64 IS NOT LINK-ONLY. Makefile:209 clears EXTRA_CFLAGS after this file is
# included, so the compile half cannot live here; src/build-variant.sh greps for
# MEMORY64=1 and passes EXTRA_CFLAGS=-sMEMORY64=1 as a make command-line
# variable. The same grep drives src/fetch-deps.sh, because linking a wasm64
# php-src against a warm wasm32 libxml2.a fails at wasm-ld hours in.
#
# IT LINKS. Run 32690008621, build (wasm64) success in 11m38s. Only the notify
# job failed, correctly: CONSUMER_VARIANTS is control85 and this run published
# wasm64. Renaming to wasm64.rc is a matter of whether it should cost a push,
# not of whether it builds.
#
# THE SIZE OBJECTION IS DEAD, MEASURED RATHER THAN MODELLED. raw 12,563,711
# against wasm32's 12,218,393 (+345,318, +2.83%), and at the shipping
# --ultra -22 that is 2,720,787 against 2,659,563: +61,224 zstd bytes into
# 220,027 of headroom, so it fits with ~158,803 to spare. The data section grows
# 3,011,523 -> 3,103,484, +3.05%.
#
# WHAT ACTUALLY REFUSES IT IS VRZNO, NOT MEMORY. Measured by pointing the
# consumer's vitest seam at this binary (DRUPFLARE_ABI=wasm64), in two steps:
#
#   1. emscripten's toIndexType feature-probes with
#      new WebAssembly.Memory({initial:1n,index:"i64"}), which workerd REFUSES,
#      so it silently degrades to the identity and every wasmTable.get() throws
#      "Cannot convert <n> to a BigInt". This is a false negative in the probe,
#      not a missing capability: replacing that IIFE with `i=>BigInt(i)` in the
#      glue gets past it, and the glue is JavaScript, so it costs no rebuild.
#   2. Past it, PHP starts (_pib_init returns) and vrzno fails the same way at
#      _vrzno_expose_create_object_for_target. Its embedded JS declares pointer
#      arguments as ccall argType "number" -- true under ILP32 and a lie under
#      LP64 -- across 59 Module.ccall sites. Porting those is the remaining work
#      and it lives in php-wasm's vrzno, not in this file.
#
# So the open question is no longer "does a Drupal heap fit at 64-bit zend_long".
# That measurement is still unmade, and it CANNOT be made until vrzno marshals
# pointers correctly, because every Host::call goes through it.

PHP_VERSION=8.5

MAIN_MODULE=0
ASYNCIFY=0
OPTIMIZE=2
INITIAL_MEMORY=96MB

WITH_VRZNO=1
WITH_LIBXML=static
WITH_DOM=static
WITH_SIMPLEXML=static
WITH_XML=static
WITH_YAML=static
WITH_ZLIB=static

WITH_CTYPE=1
WITH_FILTER=1
WITH_SESSION=1
WITH_TOKENIZER=1

WITH_BCMATH=0
WITH_CALENDAR=0
WITH_EXIF=0

WITH_ICONV=0
WITH_MBSTRING=0
WITH_ONIGURUMA=0
WITH_SQLITE=0
WITH_GD=0
WITH_LIBPNG=0
WITH_LIBJPEG=0
WITH_FREETYPE=0
WITH_LIBWEBP=0
WITH_LIBZIP=0
WITH_PHAR=0
WITH_XMLREADER=0
WITH_XMLWRITER=0
WITH_INTL=0
WITH_TIDY=0
WITH_SDL=0
WITH_OPENSSL=0
WITH_PDO_PGLITE=0
WITH_PDO_CFD1=0
WITH_WAITLINE=0

# opcache is compiled in; file_cache_only is set at runtime from the worker ini.
# The autoconf shared-memory allowlist needs no wasm64 entry: build-static.sh
# forces php_cv_shm_mmap_anon=yes by substitution, which is triple-independent.
CONFIGURE_FLAGS+= --enable-opcache

# --host FORCES CROSS MODE. emconfigure passes none, so autoconf answers
# "checking whether we are cross compiling" by RUNNING a test binary under node,
# which cannot execute a memory64 module without a flag. Measured on run
# 32685347574: libxml2 died with "cannot run C compiled programs" before any
# object was built, and php-src's own configure reaches the same wall.
#
# The triple names wasm32 deliberately. It decides which TESTS are skipped, not
# the ABI, which comes from -sMEMORY64=1 below and from EXTRA_CFLAGS; every size
# check autoconf makes is compile-time and stays correct either way. Naming
# wasm64-unknown-emscripten trades this failure for "invalid configuration" on
# any config.sub older than the triple.
CONFIGURE_FLAGS+= --host=wasm32-unknown-emscripten

EXTRA_FLAGS+= -s MEMORY64=1
